---
import PublicLaunchShell from "../components/PublicLaunchShell.astro";
---

<PublicLaunchShell
  eyebrow="Organization account"
  title="Enter an organization without making identity the role system."
  summary="This surface begins an organization-oriented journey while preserving the boundary between verified identity, organization membership, product roles, and resource authorization."
  host="org.ores-shared-auth.com"
>
  <section class="surface">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <h2>Membership is a separate proof.</h2>
      <p>
        A valid Shared Auth session is necessary but not sufficient. The target
        product must resolve the selected organization, membership status,
        role, and resource policy independently.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="form-layout">
      <aside class="notice">
        <h2>Organization guardrails</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Email-domain matching is discovery only, never membership authority.</li>
          <li>Invitations and verified memberships must resolve to immutable principals.</li>
          <li>Switching organizations requires an explicit product-local authorization decision.</li>
        </ul>
      </aside>
      <article class="form-panel">
        <h2>Continue through Shared Auth</h2>
        <p>
          Authenticate first, then let the destination application present its
          organization chooser and enforce its own authorization rules.
        </p>
        <div class="action-row">
          <a class="button" href="https://auth.ores-shared-auth.com">Open authentication</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href="https://app.ores-shared-auth.com">Choose another entry</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</PublicLaunchShell>
